VALUES ('redis-patterns', 'Redis Patterns: Cache, Sessions, Rate Limits & Leaderboards', 'Use Redis for what it is good at without trusting it with what it is not: data structures chosen by access pattern, cache-aside with TTLs, sessions, rate limits and sorted-set leaderboards, with PostgreSQL as the source of truth, invalidation that does not drift, and scores that survive duplicate and out-of-order events.', 'An advanced course for backend developers who already have Redis in production and want to stop being surprised by it. Every lesson starts from an incident on the CodeDev learning platform - a course price that stayed wrong for an hour after an edit, a leaderboard that lost every score when Redis restarted, a late event that overwrote a newer score, a login flood that took the API down, a hot key that melted the cache when it expired - and fixes it with a pattern you can test: choosing strings, hashes, sorted sets and streams, cache-aside with TTL, session keys, fixed and sliding window rate limits, invalidation, the source of truth, top N and rank, versioned score updates, rebuilding from the event log, stampedes and hot keys, and operating memory, eviction and persistence. 12 lessons with True/False quizzes on real commands, logs and timelines, and TypeScript challenges graded by hidden tests on an in-memory Redis model.', 'https://res.cloudinary.com/dex6q1cqh/image/upload/c_limit,w_1600/f_auto,q_auto/v1793020062/codedev/courses/redis-patterns/cover', 'advanced'::level_enum, 400, 'CodeDev Engineering Team', 0, 0, 150,
