Statement: "Remembering processed event ids with SET lb:seen:<eventId> 1 NX EX 172800, and skipping the event when that SET returns nil, is enough to stop both u_2041 and u_3307 from going backwards."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. It fixes u_2041, because the late write was a redelivery of the same message (evt_b07), whose id would already be marked. It does not fix u_3307: evt_e40 (version 10) and evt_e31 (version 9) are two different events, each delivered once, and the older one simply arrived last. Stopping that needs a version check: apply an event only if its version is higher than the version last applied for that learner (for example a field in the hash lb:version), and never let a stale event decrease the score. The common misconception is that idempotency also gives ordering. The two checks answer different questions: is this the same message again, and is this message older than what I already have.', 5, 5
