Statement: "A replay test that feeds the six logged deliveries, in the logged order and with a consumer restart after evt_b07''s first delivery, to the consumer on an empty Redis and then compares ZSCORE lb:global with learner_score.total for both learners, fails on the current consumer and passes after the fix."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. On the current consumer the replay ends with u_2041 at 1240 and u_3307 at 990, while learner_score says 1310 and 1025, so the comparison fails. After the fix the redelivery of evt_b07 is skipped as a duplicate and evt_e31 as stale, and both scores match the database. The restart in the replay matters: a fix that remembers ids or versions in the consumer''s memory forgets them on restart and fails, while state kept in Redis survives. Comparing Redis with the source of truth, not eyeballing the leaderboard, is the verification; the same comparison, run on a sample of learners every few minutes in production, is the drift alarm.', 6, 5
