WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_rdp_421'), 'API log and metrics, Tuesday 19:00 (5 API instances, PostgreSQL pool of 20 connections per instance):
18:59:59.990 cache hit  course:detail:nodejs-api-security  (TTL left 0.01 s)
19:00:00.004 cache miss course:detail:nodejs-api-security -> load from PostgreSQL
19:00:00.006 cache miss course:detail:nodejs-api-security -> load from PostgreSQL
... 1,897 "cache miss" lines for this key between 19:00:00.000 and 19:00:01.000 ...
19:00:01.412 cache miss course:detail:nodejs-api-security -> load failed: timeout acquiring a connection (pool 20/20)

INFO stats, delta over 19:00:00-19:00:01:  keyspace_misses +1912   keyspace_hits +2210
pg_stat_statements, delta over the same second:
  query: SELECT ... FROM course c JOIN lesson l ... WHERE c.slug = $1   calls +100   mean_exec_time 182 ms
pg_stat_activity: 100 active, 0 idle (before 19:00: 9 active)
GET /courses/:slug  p99 41 ms -> 6.8 s

Statement: "This is a cache stampede: almost all the extra load comes from one key that expired while it was in heavy use, and every request that missed it tried to run the same query."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The log shows 1,897 misses for one key in the second after its TTL ran out, and Redis counts about as many misses in total, so the misses are not spread over many keys. Every miss followed cache-aside to the letter - miss, load, store - so every concurrent request tried to load the same row: only 100 got a connection (5 instances x 20), the rest timed out waiting for the pool. Before 19:00 the same traffic cost 9 active connections because the key absorbed it. The common misconception is to read this as "PostgreSQL is too slow" or "we need a bigger pool": a bigger pool lets more identical queries run at once and makes the database slower for everyone.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_rdp_421') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
